"""Record the November 3 controller correction without rewriting earlier results."""
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];D=R/'docs';p=D/'dev-log/index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
entry='''<section class="entry" id="responsive-controls" aria-labelledby="responsive-controls-title"><p class="date">3 November 2026 · Input cancellation and contextual traversal</p><h2 id="responsive-controls-title">Separate game input timing from a generated performance</h2>
<p>The creator reported that Alt evade could feel stuck, C played a static kneeling pose, Space could not interrupt either stance/action, and another mouse click could not restart a punch. These were controller failures. The old controller rejected new actions while busy and used the entire roughly six-second performance as its action lock; crouch waited for a full multi-second transition. More generated clips would not repair that behavior.</p>
<p>The new rule is latest explicit action wins. Evade uses a 0.32-second, collision-limited displacement burst. Fresh WASD movement, C, another action or Space cancels it immediately. LMB alternates jab/cross and every click restarts an action, including the click that captures the pointer. Space preempts punches. Attack sampling uses selected active windows at short authored durations, with a 65 ms pose blend. The original complete clips, source hashes, seeds, preview identities and review histories are retained. These windows are diagnostic candidates selected from source motion landmarks; they are not proof of correct combat technique or smooth acceleration.</p>
<p>Single C immediately selects crouch locomotion, with a held support pose while stationary. A quick C C within 300 ms holds the original crouch-down ending as a static kneeling/seiza pose. Movement leaves seiza into crouch. Space jumps immediately from crouch or seiza when there is standing clearance; a tunnel roof must still block it. A normal second C toggles out of crouch. The live game no longer needs to play the complete enter-crouch performance before accepting another input.</p>
<p>Browser modifier follow-up: Ctrl itself is not crouch, but the old key listener treated Ctrl+C as plain C while the browser also received Copy. Ctrl/Command browser shortcuts now bypass gameplay and clear held input; they cannot crouch, kneel, attack, move, pause or start recording. The explicit Ctrl+Space high-jump exception remains. Tests cover modifier key events, actual Ctrl+C presses, consecutive C C isolation and ordinary crouch-to-jump afterward.</p>
<p>Physical flight now has its own lifetime, separate from the animation action. Replacing an airborne animation cannot suspend gravity. Jump anticipation is 65 ms, followed by the existing source takeoff/air/landing mapping. Step-off ledges fall under gravity. Late asynchronous clip loads carry generation tokens, so an old attack cannot return after the user has already requested a jump. Critical clips are warmed in parallel; a cold visual asset can still arrive late, but its request no longer locks gameplay.</p>
<p>Space also tests the environment in the intended movement/facing direction. Close, explicitly tagged low barriers select a vault; reachable tagged walls with free standing room select a climb onto the top. Other cases use the normal speed-sensitive jump. Ctrl+Space forces a normal high jump. The blue training wall and gold barrier have a <a href="../kimodo-game/?controls=hybrid&amp;course=traversal">direct traversal-yard starting link</a>; the HUD previews the selected Space action. Surface range, height, approach direction, destination occupancy and the swept route are checked. Roofs, benches, terminals and perimeter walls cannot become climb targets by proximity alone.</p>
<p>These traversals are authored root trajectories driven by generated skeletal poses, not learned collision avoidance or a physical climbing policy. The mantle approaches the ledge, briefly guides the hands toward its edge with a fixed-length two-bone solve, lifts, crosses and settles on top. Source pelvis lift is bounded to avoid adding height twice. Vaults lift, cross and land. A blocked route aborts into gravity. Exact hand/foot attachment, mesh-level clearance, multiple ledge heights and visual contact quality remain research tasks. Compare is an offset pose mirror; only the selected character interacts with the course.</p>
<p>Pickup/putdown attach/release events are independent of action completion: cancelling before pickup leaves the box on the ground, cancelling after attachment keeps it carried, and cancelling after release leaves it placed. Character recordings still exclude prop geometry and trajectories. The guided course now cues vaults nearer the barriers and completes in roughly 97 simulated seconds. This supersedes the earlier tour timing; it does not alter the original source performances.</p>
<p class="evidence">Validation covers actual keyboard/mouse input, both C08 and B-REK43, repeated click/replacement, single/double C, crouch/seiza jumps, delayed-load cancellation, vault/mantle landing, ceiling and boundary rejection, committed prop events and finite recorded poses. Separate regressions cover all 376 clips, review persistence/export, controller presets, four viewport layouts and the full guided tour. <a href="https://github.com/jelaludo/c08-motion-lab/blob/main/research/kimodo/responsive-controls-validation.json">Responsive input evidence</a> · <a href="../kimodo-game/action-profiles.json">Authored source windows</a> · <a href="../kimodo-game/controls.html">Updated control study</a>. Technical checks and inspected still poses do not establish final visual acceptance.</p><a class="back-top" href="#top">Back to entry index</a></section>'''
if 'id="responsive-controls"' not in s:
 s=s.replace('<ol><li><a href="#kimodo-publication">','<ol><li><a href="#responsive-controls"><span class="number">32</span>Separate game input timing from a generated performance<span class="date-small">3 November 2026 · Cancellation and traversal</span></a></li><li><a href="#kimodo-publication">',1)
 marker='<section class="entry" id="kimodo-publication"';assert marker in s;s=s.replace(marker,entry+marker,1)
s=s.replace('latest creator feedback from 2 November','latest creator feedback from 3 November')
p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
p=D/'index.html';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8').replace('31 entries · methods','32 entries · methods');p.write_text(s,encoding='utf-8',newline='\n')
print('Added entry 32: responsive game controls and traversal limits.')
